 # Changelog
 
+## Unreleased
+
+- Ticket assignment: `PUT /tickets/:id/assignee` assigns an open or in-progress ticket to an agent, or unassigns it with
+  `null`; the agent is notified. Tickets show their `assignee`, `GET /tickets` filters on `assignee`, and `list` shows it.
+- A ticket listing with several filters now keeps only the tickets that match all of them (it kept those matching any).
+- `POST /tickets/import` creates up to 5000 tickets at once, all or none, for the move from the old tracker.
+
+- Due times: a ticket is due its creation time plus the response time of its priority (`RESPONSE_HOURS_*`, 4, 24, 72
+  and 168 hours by default), set once and never moved. With `DUE_TIMES=on` tickets show `due` and `GET /tickets` filters
+  on `overdue=true` (open and in-progress tickets past their due time). The data file gains a `due` per ticket, and the
+  tickets already in it get theirs at the first start, whether `DUE_TIMES` is on or not. The file stays version 1, so
+  release 1.4.0 still starts on it.
+
 ## 1.4.0 (2025-09-15)
 
 - The operator command line, `bin/tickets.js` (`list`, `show`), and the weekly report, `scripts/weekly-report.js`.
